    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.doc\n\n### Description\n\nFor starters, thanks for all the work you do on this plugin.\n\nI decided to give mini.doc a try and called `MiniDoc.generate()` without arguments. I noticed that your docs were different from what I got, mine having extra lines at the top. Upon investigating your repo, I found this neat little tidbit at `scripts/minidoc.lua`:\n\n```lua\nlocal hooks = vim.deepcopy(MiniDoc.default_hooks)\n\nhooks.write_pre = function(lines)\n        -- Remove first two lines with `======` and `------` delimiters to comply\n        -- with `:h local-additions` template\n        table.remove(lines, 1)\n        table.remove(lines, 1)\n        return lines\nend\n```\n\nGiven that it exists to comply with a built-in feature, I think it should be the default. What do you think?",
